name 'designing-reliable-apps-postassessment-q12_2026'

question 'A developer wraps a fetch request in try...catch. The fetch succeeds, but the code inside the try block that processes the returned data throws a TypeError. What happens?'

wrong 'The try block suppresses the TypeError and returns undefined to the calling function'
wrong 'The fetch is automatically retried because the original network request succeeded'
right 'The catch block runs and handles the TypeError, preventing the app from crashing'
wrong 'The catch block is skipped entirely because the fetch itself completed without errors'

allow_multiple_attempts true

